<b>Your jokes suck, David!</b>

12:48.590 --> 12:49.490
<b>Bane!</b>

12:49.490 --> 12:53.070
<b>Reiji Shinjo</b>

12:49.870 --> 12:52.640
<b>I'd love to visit her house.</b>

12:53.070 --> 12:55.330
<b>And that's all we have time for.</b>

12:55.330 --> 12:58.170
<b>Press the button of the person
 you're most attracted to!</b>

13:10.590 --> 13:12.180
<b>Wh-What the heck?</b>

13:10.590 --> 13:12.010
<b>Ryo Shishido</b>

13:12.010 --> 13:12.550
<b>Ryo Shishido</b>

13:12.550 --> 13:17.680
<b>Ryo Shishido</b>

13:12.700 --> 13:17.680
<b>Well, this is a surprise! 
It seems the ladies all chose Shishido.</b>

13:17.850 --> 13:18.930
<b>Wait a second.</b>

13:18.930 --> 13:23.640
<b>I voted for Shusuke, because it would've 
been sad if nobody chose him.</b>

13:24.610 --> 13:25.860
<b>Thanks, sis.</b>

13:30.110 --> 13:32.080
<b>Wh-What's going on?</b>

13:40.610 --> 13:43.030
<b>It looks like the machine blew up.</b>

13:43.370 --> 13:47.460
<b>Yup, knew it. There's no way 
everyone would choose him.</b>

13:47.460 --> 13:49.010
<b>What's <i>that</i> supposed to mean?</b>

13:49.010 --> 13:49.860
<b>Like it sounds.</b>

13:49.860 --> 13:54.000
<b>Um, Ms. Hanamura. Who did you choose?</b>

13:55.210 --> 13:58.390
<b>Shinjo, asking that is against the rules.</b>

14:13.450 --> 14:18.570
<b><i>Onto our main event of the day:
the interscholastic obstacle relay race.</i></b>

14:19.310 --> 14:22.140
<b><i>Let's briefly go over the rules.</i></b>

14:22.360 --> 14:26.830
<b><i>Students will first do 
a lap of a 400-meter track,</i></b>

14:26.830 --> 14:30.610
<b><i>then complete various checkpoint
tasks to reach the finish line.</i></b>

14:31.550 --> 14:39.050
Prize

14:32.260 --> 14:36.730
<b>The winning team will receive top-quality 
tennis equipment for their entire team.</b>

14:36.730 --> 14:41.880
<b>They will also receive a gold lifetime 
membership card, allowing free access</b>

14:41.880 --> 14:47.930
<b>to 200 tennis courts around Japan,
all run by the Atobe family.</b>

14:48.490 --> 14:50.810
<b>Top-quality tennis equipment, huh?</b>

14:51.650 --> 14:52.910
<b>This one's ours!</b>

14:53.650 --> 14:54.870
<b>I'll overthrow this race.</b>

14:55.580 --> 14:57.490
<b>I'm gonna win, no matter what!</b>

14:57.920 --> 15:03.700
<b><i>Okay, the race is about to begin. 
Competitors, please take your places.</i></b>

15:05.180 --> 15:06.250
<b>Hey, Tezuka.</b>

15:07.350 --> 15:09.890
<b>Victory will be mine.</b>

15:11.890 --> 15:13.700
<b>Let's all give it our best.</b>

15:29.910 --> 15:31.020
<b><i>You may go.</i></b>

15:34.810 --> 15:36.860
<b>I'll get in my rhythm!</b>

15:37.110 --> 15:41.060
<b><i>Wow! Just look at Fudomine's Kamio. 
What incredible speed!</i></b>

15:41.060 --> 15:43.610
<b><i>He'll reach the second runner in no time.</i></b>

15:47.950 --> 15:51.560
<b><i>Oh no! Kamio fell over!</i></b>

15:51.560 --> 15:54.210
<b><i>That allows Rokkaku Junior 
High to take the lead.</i></b>

15:57.920 --> 16:00.880
<b><i>The sash gets passed to the second runner.</i></b>

16:01.450 --> 16:03.070
<b><i>Rokkaku Junior High is in first,</i></b>

16:03.070 --> 16:05.880
<b><i>followed by Yamabuki Junior High,
then Hyotei Academy.</i></b>

16:07.510 --> 16:11.360
<b><i>Next, the competitors must wade
through this pool of potato starch</i></b>

16:11.360 --> 16:13.360
<b><i>and find a candy in order to move on.</i></b>

16:13.530 --> 16:15.470
<b>This is my kind of game.</b>

16:24.760 --> 16:29.140
<b><i>Rokkaku Junior High's Itsuki
 found the candy super fast!</i></b>

16:29.140 --> 16:29.720
<b>Found one!</b>

16:29.720 --> 16:30.660
<b>Me, too!</b>

16:30.920 --> 16:35.720
<b><i>Itsuki blew away too much potato starch. 
He helped out his opponents, too.</i></b>

16:36.820 --> 16:38.670
<b><i>I got the candy!</i></b>

16:39.770 --> 16:42.050
<b><i>The course now goes steeply uphill.</i></b>

16:44.580 --> 16:46.600
<b><i>It's a very long course.</i></b>

16:46.930 --> 16:49.790
<b><i>Who will reach the top first?</i></b>

16:55.090 --> 16:58.980
<b><i>He made it! Seigaku's Inui has 
completed the checkpoint task!</i></b>

16:58.980 --> 17:03.130
<b><i>If I can keep up this pace, 
the probability of us winning is 95%.</i></b>

17:08.700 --> 17:10.430
<b><i>No one does it like the Atobe family!</i></b>

17:10.430 --> 17:14.050
<b><i>They've made an artificial snow-covered 
mountain using a snow machine!</i></b>

17:17.470 --> 17:19.320
<b>L-Logic doesn't apply.</b>

17:23.050 --> 17:26.930
<b><i>The competitors are sliding smoothly 
down the snow mountain course.</i></b>

17:36.050 --> 17:38.010
<b><i>The battle is fierce.</i></b>

17:38.250 --> 17:41.010
<b><i>Next up, it's shoulder wars.</i></b>

17:41.400 --> 17:42.650
<b>Let's go.</b>

17:46.090 --> 17:50.420
<b><i>It looks like everyone's forgotten it's a race
 and they're going after their sashes.</i></b>

17:50.420 --> 17:53.890
<b>I'll crush each and every one of you!</b>

17:56.050 --> 17:57.740
<b>Huh? Someone lost their swimsuit.</b>

17:58.180 --> 17:59.300
<b>Prepare for war!</b>

17:59.660 --> 18:00.750
<b>Wait, Momo.</b>

18:01.010 --> 18:04.850
<b>We should head to the finish line
instead of fighting our opponents.</b>

18:05.110 --> 18:06.050
<b>Roger that!</b>

18:07.940 --> 18:09.430
<b>Turn around, Momoshiro!</b>

18:09.430 --> 18:11.020
<b>Gotcha, Viper.</b>

18:13.610 --> 18:16.220
<b>Echizen! Over here!</b>

18:16.390 --> 18:18.210
<b>Captain!</b>

18:23.170 --> 18:25.510
<b><i>Seigaku's anchor is Captain Tezuka.</i></b>

18:25.510 --> 18:26.450
<b>Oh no you don't!</b>

18:26.880 --> 18:29.360
<b><i>And Hyotei's anchor is Atobe.</i></b>

18:29.770 --> 18:33.810
<b><i>Who will win? Seigaku or Hyotei?</i></b>

18:33.810 --> 18:37.490
<b><i>Neither is giving an inch. 
It's going down to the wire.</i></b>

19:08.920 --> 19:11.730
<b>Tezuka!</b>

19:29.690 --> 19:30.490
<b>Atobe...</b>

19:33.620 --> 19:35.270
<b>Don't misinterpret this.</b>

19:35.580 --> 19:40.410
<b>I just can't let someone get hurt 
at an event I'm hosting, that's all.</b>

19:45.540 --> 19:46.490
<b>Is your leg hurt?</b>

19:47.850 --> 19:49.490
<b>I just twisted it a little.</b>

19:50.590 --> 19:53.500
<b>It's nothing compared to your arm injury.</b>

19:58.560 --> 19:59.380
<b>Tezuka...</b>

19:59.960 --> 20:01.000
<b>No more words.</b>

20:30.620 --> 20:35.870
<b>Seigaku's
Principal</b>

20:30.620 --> 20:35.870
<b>Principal Ishikawa</b>

20:35.870 --> 20:37.040
<b>Seigaku's
Principal</b>

20:35.870 --> 20:37.540
<b>Principal Ishikawa</b>

20:37.040 --> 20:37.540
<b>Seigaku's
Principal</b>

20:37.540 --> 20:38.880
<b>Seigaku's
Principal</b>

20:37.730 --> 20:38.870
<b>Congratulations.</b>

20:44.420 --> 20:46.290
<b>It's a tie this time.</b>

20:49.170 --> 20:51.350
<b>We'll settle this another day.</b>

21:02.810 --> 21:04.930
<b>Let's dance!</b>

21:49.770 --> 21:52.410
<b>She's Kabaji's older sister, right?</b>

21:53.130 --> 21:57.610
<b>From the interviews I've done, 
I learned that Kabaji's been down lately.</b>

21:58.200 --> 22:01.050
<b>His older sister, who he's been 
close to since childhood,</b>

22:01.050 --> 22:04.840
<b>or in other words, the lady 
he's dancing with right now,</b>

22:04.840 --> 22:07.130
<b>is getting married soon.</b>

22:08.630 --> 22:11.270
<b>Your ability to gather 
information is impressive.</b>

22:11.270 --> 22:18.350
<b>You came up with this extravagant
 event to lift Kabaji's spirits.</b>

22:20.330 --> 22:22.350
<b>That's not all. There's one more reason.</b>

22:23.970 --> 22:26.280
<b>Today's his birthday.</b>

22:27.440 --> 22:31.330
<b>But I hope you won't 
include that in your article.</b>

22:31.910 --> 22:35.030
<b>Kabaji's more sensitive than he looks.</b>

22:35.570 --> 22:40.990
<b>Don't worry. Sticking our noses into your 
private lives is against editorial policy.</b>

22:45.810 --> 22:46.710
<b>How was it?</b>

22:46.970 --> 22:49.510
<b>Did you make good memories with her, Kabaji?</b>

22:49.510 --> 22:50.670
<b>Yes.</b>

22:50.680 --> 22:53.500
<b>But there's something 
I've been meaning to tell you.</b>

22:55.550 --> 22:58.690
<b>Today's not my birthday.</b>

23:08.730 --> 23:14.730
<b>Well, this year, it is. Isn't that right?</b>

23:16.320 --> 23:17.370
<b>Yes.</b>

23:18.170 --> 23:23.420
<b>And this festival is a gift from me to you.</b>

23:27.850 --> 23:30.380
<b>That concludes today's event.</b>

23:31.160 --> 23:35.380
<b>There were a few hiccups, 
but I'm glad the festival ended safely.</b>

23:35.730 --> 23:40.350
<b>And it was all thanks to my ability 
to plan and execute such an event.</b>

23:40.540 --> 23:43.530
<b>How can he be so full of himself like that?</b>

23:43.530 --> 23:47.410
<b>He deserves it. We all had fun.</b>

23:49.190 --> 23:52.060
<b>I wish I could've spent 
more time with Prince Ryoma.</b>

23:52.060 --> 23:53.120
<b>Yeah.</b>

23:53.370 --> 23:56.730
<b>But it's not over just yet.</b>

23:57.830 --> 24:01.640
<b>There's an after-party 
and everyone here is invited.</b>

24:02.940 --> 24:04.530
<b>Did you hear that, Tomo?</b>

24:04.830 --> 24:06.890
<b>It'll be at my house.</b>

24:07.460 --> 24:10.580
<b>And I'm not letting any of you
 leave early. You got that?</b>

24:12.910 --> 24:13.610
<b>Coach.</b>

24:16.650 --> 24:17.810
<b>You may go.</b>

24:32.680 --> 24:33.890
<b>Get down!</b>

24:50.300 --> 24:53.810
<b>Hey, Gakuto, the venue's moving.</b>

25:23.450 --> 25:29.580
<b>Kabaji, 
\h\hthanks for 
\h\h\heverything</b>

25:29.580 --> 25:32.960
<b>Kabaji, 
\h\hthanks for 
\h\h\heverything</b>
